0-17ffca1d2a08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517948 #edb/ref 1080 "$y$ is inversely proportional to $x$ with a constant of variation $k=4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517948 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186517948 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f07b6d5a-a5a6-55bc-bf86-f6c9b061a44a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517598 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517610 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518069 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d155659c-c17e-5eca-b3d0-23cecfde70bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518075 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518075 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518075 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518075 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518075 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d7f79e97-d630-5908-a05a-ee3b6a7eb854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517522 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517712 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186517948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186517817 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518091 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f89a1044-5822-5030-9b03-184a93ebec0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518108 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518108 #edb/ref 1069 "q-115488" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518108 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518108 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the table below. Which of the following is a true statement about the relationship between $x$ and $y?$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $0.5$ | $20$ |\n| $2$ | $5$ |\n| $4$ | $2.5$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518108 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "11ab4bcc-ff94-5b73-9790-5edd61c08193" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518108 #edb/ref 1074 "If $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ then we must have\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nfor some constant $k.$ Note that we can rewrite the above equation as follows.\n\n$$\nx\\cdot y=k\n$$\n\nSo, we will compute $x\\cdot y=k$ for each row in the table. If we get the same value of $k$ for each row, then we can conclude that $y$ is inversely proportional to $x.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $x\\cdot y=k$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0.5$ | $20$ | $0.5\\cdot 20=10$ |\n| $2$ | $5$ | $2\\cdot 5=10$ |\n| $4$ | $2.5$ | $4\\cdot 2.5=10$ |\n\nThe results are all the same: in each row, we have $k=10.$ Therefore, $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ and the constant of variation is $k=10.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518113 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518075 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518113 #edb/ref 1069 "q-217248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518113 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518113 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose that $y$ varies inversely with $x$ and that $y=\\frac{3}{4}$ when $x=12.$ Then, if $x=\\frac{1}{3},$ $y=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518113 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1c37fb77-7c99-58f3-b32e-45223dbee74b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518113 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nWe are told that $y=\\frac{3}{4}$ when $x=12.$ We substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{4} & =\\frac{k}{12} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot 12 & =k \\\\ 9 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the inverse variation is given by \n\n$$\ny=\\frac{9}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the value of $x=\\frac{1}{3}$ into this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{9}{(\\frac{1}{3})} \\\\  & =9÷(\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =9\\cdot (\\frac{3}{1}) \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518200 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186518069 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518200 #edb/ref 1069 "q-115589" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518200 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518200 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/96/9674072fe2d9f831635dfd2994b97ea6e9603dd576586f80e4b1b2e6a2373564.png)\n\nThe graph above shows the relationship between $x$ and $y.$ Given that $y$ is inversely proportional to $x,$ find the value of $a.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518200 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf708341-904e-56d2-b929-e74c203d19a7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518200 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nIn the graph, we notice a point with $y=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $x=5.$ We substitute this data into the equation to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{k}{5} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5 & =k \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse variation equation that relates $y$ and $x$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{(\\frac{5}{2})}{x}=\\frac{5}{2x}.\n$$\n\nFrom the graph, we also have that $y=\\frac{5}{2}$ when $x=a.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{5}{2a} \\\\ 10a & =10 \\\\ a & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518249 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518249 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "47c6ba42-9469-510d-8375-d74fdf459167" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518249 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518200 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518273 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "946d1bf9-981b-5a6b-afb7-e0f580f11f36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518273 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518308 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186518249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518308 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e3cb0b4d-15dc-5baa-9658-0e5055d4371c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186518308 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186518108 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
